---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the Ethotechnics framework"
  description="What Ethotechnics is, where it comes from, who authored it, and how the Institute and Studio fit together."
>
  <section class="stack-lg">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the framework</p>
    <h1>What Ethotechnics is and where it comes from</h1>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Ethotechnics is a governance and care-infrastructure framework for designing, operating, and
      auditing high-stakes sociotechnical systems. It combines enforceable standards, defined
      vocabulary, diagnostics, and implementation patterns to make accountability operational.
    </p>
    <p>
      The framework was authored by <strong>Kanav Jain</strong> and is maintained through the
      Ethotechnics Institute as an open, versioned public resource.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-lg">
    <p class="eyebrow">Institute + Studio</p>
    <h2>How the Institute and Studio differ</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>Ethotechnics Institute</strong> publishes the open commons: standards, glossary,
      ontology, API, diagnostics, and field notes. These materials are free to use, cite, and build
      on.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <strong>Ethotechnics Studio</strong> provides paid engagements, facilitation, and advisory
      support for teams applying the framework in live environments.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/">Visit the Institute homepage →</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
      <a href="https://ethotechnics.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        Visit Ethotechnics Studio →
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-lg">
    <p class="eyebrow">Read the foundations</p>
    <h2>Foundational essays and entry points</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/field-notes">Field notes and essays</a></li>
      <li><a href="/research">Research program overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="/standards/core-axioms">Core axioms</a></li>
      <li><a href="/glossary">Glossary (recommended starting point)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-lg">
    <p class="eyebrow">Citation guidance</p>
    <h2>How to cite Ethotechnics</h2>
    <p>
      Ethotechnics Institute materials are published under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Jain, K. (2025). <em>Ethotechnics: A governance and care-infrastructure framework for
      high-stakes systems.</em> Ethotechnics Institute. https://ethotechnics.org
    </blockquote>
    <p>Individual glossary entries and patterns include their own citation metadata.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
